  "summary": "Predicted structures now feed screening and design, so ensembles, pose metrics, membrane checks and confidence filters need scrutiny.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a focus on infrastructure and evaluation for structure-based ligand modeling from predicted or curated structures. ANTIOCH-VS chains ColabFold subsampling, AF2RAVE MD ensembles, docking and consensus ranking into an open pipeline from sequence to hits. PocketVec descriptors map 51,535 druggable human pockets to select diverse Target 2035 targets. CARVE scores protein-glycan poses with oRMSD, irRMSD and Fnat across 1,974 complexes. Two items probe the limits of predicted structures: a membrane-geometry audit of about 189k AlphaFold-Multimer transmembrane complexes, and a lanmodulin study showing pTM and ipLDDT poorly select functional REE-binding designs. The summaries give no head-to-head accuracy comparisons for the pipeline; novelty lies in resource construction, target selection and evaluation design.",
